WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.662
"How to Prevent Skin Cancer with Diet"

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.900
Millions of skin cancers
are diagnosed every year,

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.480
the most common cancer
in the United States.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.720
I've covered the single
most important thing we can do-

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.300
protect against exposure
to UV radiation,

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.120
and just did a video
on a supplement that might help.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.220
What about dietary protection?

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.820
The first study to elucidate
the effect of diet

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.820
on UV-induced tumors
found that high-fat diets

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.980
accelerated tumor formation
in mice.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.780
Within six months of UV,

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.020
fifty percent of the high-fat
fed mice had tumors

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.840
compared to only 16
in the control-fed group.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.300
Encouragingly,
switching the mice

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.100
to a low-fat diet
after the exposure

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.520
was able to negate the tumor
exacerbating high-fat effects.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.640
In people, a dietary pattern

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.380
characterized by meat
and fat consumption

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.900
was associated
with up to a near quadrupling

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.940
of squamous cell
carcinoma risk,

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:58.920
the second most common type
of skin cancer,

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.720
whereas a vegetable
and fruit pattern

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.940
was associated
with a halving of risk

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:06.180
(apparently driven largely
by the intake of greens).

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:10.140
All we needed now
was to randomize people

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.820
to low-fat diets
and see if cancer

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.680
could be prevented
in people too,

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:17.220
and, thanks to National
Cancer Institute funding

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.960
and a Veteran Affairs
research team,

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.760
the striking results
were published

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.380
in the New England
Journal of Medicine.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.620
Seventy-six patients
with a history of skin cancer

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.720
(and, therefore, at high risk
of developing more)

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.840
were randomized to continue
to eat their regular diets

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.660
or switch to a quote-unquote
"low-fat" diet

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.340
of 20 percent of calories
from fat.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.400
I put low-fat in quotes

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.100
because that's actually
a high-fat diet

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.740
compared to what's normal
for our species.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.740
For millions of years,
our ancestors may have evolved

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:48.060
getting approximately
10 percent

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.440
of our calories from fat.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.180
For millions of years,

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:54.420
about 99.8 percent
of our time on Earth,

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.720
it was virtually impossible
for us to consume regularly

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.540
more than 10 to 15 percent
of calories as fat.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:04.380
So, that's a normal fat diet
for the human species.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:07.020
A low-fat diet
would be less than that.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:11.160
Though 20 percent is certainly
comparatively low fat

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:12.720
compared to the current
adult average

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.060
in the United States
of 37 percent.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:18.720
Would a drop down to 20
make a difference?

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:21.240
Researchers tracked
the appearance

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.940
of actinic keratoses,
rough scaly patches

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:26.820
that are premalignant lesions
that turn into skin cancer,

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:28.200
over the next two years.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.960
The average patient
in the control group

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.240
developed 10 lesions
in those two years,

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:35.580
compared to just three
in the lower-fat group.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:39.540
Okay, but what about
actual skin cancers?

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.460
The results were so exciting

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.500
the same team of researchers
randomized

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:44.940
hundreds
of skin cancer patients

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.320
to the same two diets.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:47.520
By the end of the study,

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.760
the skin cancer rate
was 10 times lower

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:52.380
in the lower-fat group.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:56.760
Now this is no clarion call
for SnackWell's cookies.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:59.280
Although fat appears
twice as bad,

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.340
high-refined carb consumption
was also found to be

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:04.800
significantly associated
with skin wrinkling and atrophy

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.540
among a nationwide
cross-section

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:07.440
of middle-aged women.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.300
Those who consistently have

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.580
higher than normal
fasting blood sugars

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.280
are perceived to be
nearly a half year older

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:15.240
than they really are

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:18.840
for every 18 points higher
their average blood sugars are.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.600
So, those with a prediabetic
fasting blood sugar

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.000
of like 120 milligrams
per deciliter

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.760
look about a year older
than those regularly having

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:29.460
a normal fasting blood sugar
of around 75.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:32.040
Now, the Women's Health
Initiative randomized

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.080
nearly 50,000
postmenopausal women

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.840
to a recommendation
to eat the same lower-fat diet;

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.460
yet, there was no change

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.680
in the incidence
of skin cancer.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:44.100
This is not surprising
given the poor adherence.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.340
Only 31 percent of the women
in the intervention group

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:49.260
complied with
the dietary recommendations.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:52.380
It turns out healthy diets
may only work

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:55.680
if you actually eat them.

